# agent-secrets registry — single place to wire a `pass` entry into the AI
# coding agents. Read by:
#   ~/.local/bin/hermes-secrets          (Hermes secrets.command env blob)
#   ~/.local/bin/opencode-with-secrets   (env exports before opencode starts)
#   ~/.local/bin/pi-pass-auth            (writes "!agent-secrets" command keys
#                                         into ~/.pi/agent/auth.json)
#
# Format: ENV_VAR  pass-entry  [pi-provider-id]
#   ENV_VAR        the variable the tool ecosystem knows (Hermes plugins and
#                  OpenCode built-ins read these; see the "env" list per
#                  provider in ~/.cache/opencode/models.json).
#   pi-provider-id pi's provider ID for the same key (from pi's
#                  docs/providers.md table); omit to skip pi for that entry.
#   '#' lines and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Adding a provider = add `pass insert cloud/<name>` then one line here, then
# re-run: `stow -t ~ agents` (if the registry changed), `pi-pass-auth`, and
# restart each agent. Keys never land in this repo or in any agent's store.

# --- model providers -------------------------------------------------------
ALIBABA_TOKEN_PLAN_API_KEY cloud/qwencloud          qwen-token-plan-individual
GEMINI_API_KEY             cloud/gemini_API_key      google
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY           cloud/deepseek            deepseek
OPENROUTER_API_KEY         cloud/openrouter          openrouter

# Anthropic caveat (kept from the original hermes-secrets): export as
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY only — never ANTHROPIC_TOKEN, which sits first in the
# resolution order and would shadow Claude Code OAuth. For pi the same
# reasoning applies: leave the pi-provider-id empty while ~/.claude
# credentials are in use; set it to "anthropic" only if you want the console
# key to win in pi too.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY          cloud/claude_api_dpa

# No pass entry yet — add one and uncomment (pi ID: openai):
# OPENAI_API_KEY             cloud/openai              openai

# --- tools ------------------------------------------------------------------
EXA_API_KEY                cloud/exa_api_key.el
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN         cloud/telegram_bot_token
